// Out-of-bounds slice index must PANIC at runtime (zen__idx preamble bounds guard),
// not silently return a bad pointer. Indexing a 3-element slice at 10 aborts with
// "zen: panic: slice index out of bounds" (exit 134). Guards the runtime bounds
// check — removing it passed every value/verdict case (mutation-testing HOLE 2:
// the panic was previously caught only incidentally by the fixpoint text-diff).
main = () i32 {
    xs := [1, 2, 3]
    xs[10]
}
